# logs.manifest — config owned by mod_logs (unified log retention).
#
# Layered (update-system.md phase 3):
#   • /usr/share/w/defaults/logs.conf   — W's retention default. Class managed:
#     overwritten by every update, so a changed distro default reaches machines
#     that never set their own.
#   • /usr/share/w/defaults/logs.schema — who may set each key (system-scope: one
#     user must not decide how long the machine keeps everyone's logs).
#   • /etc/w/logs.conf — this machine's DEVIATIONS only. Class override: the update
#     never touches it; `w-reset logs` drops them back to the vendor layer.
#
# The rendered files (journald 10-w-retention.conf, tmpfiles w-logs.conf, the
# logrotate global region + zz-w-catchall) are w-logs output, not tracked here:
# regenerate them with `sudo w-logs apply`.
# The logrotate.service ExecStartPre drop-in is a static W-owned system file.
#
# Format: <path>\t<class>   class: managed | override
/usr/share/w/defaults/logs.conf	managed
/usr/share/w/defaults/logs.schema	managed
/etc/w/logs.conf	override
/etc/systemd/system/logrotate.service.d/10-w-catchall-refresh.conf	managed
